// GetRateLimit invokes get-rate-limit operation.
//
// Returns the effective requests-per-minute (RPM) limit for the project identified by the verified IAM
// token. Only operators can change the limit. Canopy's deployment configuration defaults to 120 RPM
// and may be overridden per project; this is our limit, independent of any upstream provider's limits.
// A value of 0 means unlimited.
//
// All Canopy-issued API keys belonging to this project share one limit across all models in a rolling
// 60-second window. Only inference authenticated with these API keys counts: IAM project-token
// inference, internal-service inference and model listing are excluded. This management endpoint still
// requires an IAM token, not an API key.
//
// A streaming request counts once. Responses WebSocket traffic counts each `response.create`; realtime
// traffic counts each session. Admitted attempts count even if the upstream fails. Gateway retries do
// not count again, and rate-limit rejections do not consume capacity.
//
// `rpm` is the exact count of project model-call arrivals that passed the project rate limiter in the
// last 60 seconds, including attempts rejected before model admission. `tps` is the output throughput
// in tokens per second across completed project requests with reported output or reasoning tokens in
// the last 60 seconds, computed as total reported output tokens divided by total end-to-end request
// duration. TPS is observational only and is not enforced.
//
