// are null, not zero; the configured limit is still returned. When the live store is available and no
// eligible output requests completed in the last 60 seconds, `tps` is 0. Snapshots have one-second
// precision and are refreshed at least every two seconds; clients should poll every five seconds.
//
// An attempt exceeding a nonzero limit is rejected with 429 `RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`. `Retry-After` gives
// the wait in seconds. Inference rate-limit headers are `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`
// and `X-RateLimit-Reset` (Unix seconds). If Redis cannot perform the rate-limit check, inference
// fails with 503 rather than bypassing the limit. Rate-limit edits take effect within 30 seconds.
